<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
com.throne.ntfy.plist — throne-owned macOS LaunchAgent template for the
throne's phone-notification server; the mac counterpart of
throne/systemd/ntfy.service.

Not loadable as it stands: `{{THRONE_ROOT}}` (absolute path of the throne
directory) is substituted at install time, and only the rendered copy in the
user's LaunchAgents dir is a working agent. Install with:
  cd <throne root> && ./install.sh        (or ./bin/throne-cli install-services)

Enabled and bootstrapped by install-services, like its systemd twin. The
program is the same `ntfy-serve` script the linux unit runs; that script is
platform-aware (ifconfig instead of iproute2, the Tailscale.app bundle CLI,
optional GNU timeout) and runs the server as the pinned binwiederhier/ntfy
image (vendor-pins.json tools.ntfy.image, pulled by ./install.sh) under
docker or podman, whichever the host has. Tailscale is the one prerequisite
nothing here installs: ntfy is tailnet-only by design, and without a tailnet
address (or with the runtime still starting) ntfy-serve exits non-zero, so KeepAlive
relaunches it after ThrottleInterval — the same wait-and-retry boot-race
contract as the linux unit's Restart=always.

PROVEN on a real mac (2026-09-02, macOS 26 / Darwin 25.6, Docker Desktop
29): the plist parses and bootstraps, and the pinned image serves the
throne's config; see agent_docs/ntfy-phone-notifications.md for the mac
commands.

KEYS SHIPPED BELOW
  Label             a launchctl service target is built from this label
                    rather than from the filename.
  ProgramArguments  /bin/bash as a login shell so the container runtime
                    (docker under /usr/local/bin, podman under brew) and
                    `timeout` (brew coreutils, optional) resolve — launchd's
                    bare system PATH reaches neither. Output goes to
                    ~/Library/Logs/throne/ntfy.log; StandardOutPath does not
                    expand ~, hence the redirect inside the shell.
  RunAtLoad         launchd.plist(5): "This optional key is used to control
                    whether your job is launched once at the time the job is
                    loaded. The default is false."
  KeepAlive         launchd.plist(5): "The value may be set to true to
                    unconditionally keep the job alive." It stands in for the
                    linux unit's Restart=always.
  ThrottleInterval  launchd.plist(5): "by default, jobs will not be spawned
                    more than once every 10 seconds." 10 is that documented
                    default; the linux unit's RestartSec=5s is not reproduced.
  Umask             63 decimal is 0077 octal, the linux unit's UMask. Spelled
                    in decimal because launchd.plist(5) Umask says the value
                    "must be a decimal representation of the desired umask, as
                    property lists do not support encoding integers in octal."
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>Label</key>
	<string>com.throne.ntfy</string>
	<key>ProgramArguments</key>
	<array>
		<string>/bin/bash</string>
		<string>-lc</string>
		<string>mkdir -p "$HOME/Library/Logs/throne" &amp;&amp; exec {{THRONE_ROOT}}/systemd/ntfy-serve {{THRONE_ROOT}}/systemd/ntfy-server.yml &gt;&gt; "$HOME/Library/Logs/throne/ntfy.log" 2&gt;&amp;1</string>
	</array>
	<key>RunAtLoad</key>
	<true/>
	<key>KeepAlive</key>
	<true/>
	<key>ThrottleInterval</key>
	<integer>10</integer>
	<key>Umask</key>
	<integer>63</integer>
</dict>
</plist>
